<Routines>
<Routine Name="EnableInFalse" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Disabled is asserted; Outputs OFF; Valve Status shown based on feedbacks if possible, but Alarms disabled]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
OFF-SCAN (EnableIn is False) STATUS
============================================================
If this Valve is OFF-SCAN (rung is false or EnableIn is false in FBD), then:

Handle "NO MODE" Selection using the standard P_Mode AOI (EnableInFalse Routine, false scan required!).

NOTE:  IN ORDER TO AVOID USING AN "AFI" (which will generate a routine verify warning),
THIS RUNG USES AN XIC of Cfg_PCmdClear, followed by an XIO of the SAME BIT
to ensure P_Mode is SCANNED FALSE ("NO MODE").

THIS IS NOT DEAD CODE AND MUST APPEAR EXACTLY AS SHOWN FOR PROPER OPERATION!]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear)XIO(Cfg_PCmdClear)P_Mode(Mode);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[First-Come First-Served Ownership Arbitration still needs to happen, even when device is disabled.
If a requestor supplies a non-zero Owner ID and the current owner is NONE (zero),
Ownership is assigned to the requesting ID.  When that requestor sets the Owner ID back
to zero, Ownership is relinquished back to NONE.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[EQU(PSet_Owner,0) ,EQU(Val_Owner,0) ]MOV(PSet_Owner,Val_Owner);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA["Lurking" Program Commands are cleared if they are set as "Edge" triggered
(cleared by this object as received).
(Lurking Acknowledge Commands are left to perform their action.)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear)[OTU(PCmd_Close) OTU(PCmd_Open) OTU(PCmd_LiftLower) OTU(PCmd_LiftUpper) ,OTU(PCmd_SIPCavity) OTU(PCmd_SIPLower) OTU(PCmd_SIPUpper) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA["Lurking" Operator Commands are cleared, as well as Program Reset.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTU(OCmd_Close) OTU(OCmd_Open) OTU(OCmd_LiftLower) OTU(OCmd_LiftUpper) ,OTU(OCmd_SIPCavity) OTU(OCmd_SIPLower) OTU(OCmd_SIPUpper) ,OTU(OCmd_Bypass) OTU(OCmd_Check) OTU(MCmd_Disable) OTU(MCmd_Enable) ,OTU(OCmd_Reset) OTU(OCmd_ResetAckAll) OTU(PCmd_Reset) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Override Command is set to NONE.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CLR(Inp_OvrdCmd);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Since we're not processing Operator Commands, we're not READY for them either!]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTU(Rdy_Close) OTU(Rdy_Open) OTU(Rdy_LiftLower) OTU(Rdy_LiftUpper) ,OTU(Rdy_SIPCavity) OTU(Rdy_SIPLower) OTU(Rdy_SIPUpper) ,OTU(Rdy_Bypass) OTU(Rdy_Check) OTU(Rdy_Disable) OTU(Rdy_Enable) ,OTU(Rdy_Reset) OTU(Rdy_ResetAckAll) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Reset the fault condition and state hold timers.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[RES(Wrk_FailT)RES(Wrk_StateT);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Outputs are cleared when Disabled.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTU(Out_Close) OTU(Out_Open) OTU(Out_LiftLower) OTU(Out_LiftUpper) ,OTU(Out_CavityInlet) OTU(Out_CavityOutlet) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Show the valve as Disabled and Not Ready, not Available, and with no
Maintenance Bypass breadcrumb.
Show NO valve position status (none are confirmed).
Show the enumerated valve command as NONE.
Show the enumerated valve status as DISABLED.
Show the enumerated valve fault status as NONE.
Show the internal valve state as DE-ENERGIZED.

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTL(Sts_Disabled) OTL(Sts_NotRdy) OTU(Sts_Available) OTU(Sts_MaintByp) ,OTL(Nrdy_NoMode) OTU(Nrdy_Disabled) OTU(Nrdy_CfgErr) OTU(Nrdy_Intlk) ,OTU(Nrdy_Perm) OTU(Nrdy_Fail) OTU(Nrdy_IOFault) ,OTU(Sts_Closed) OTU(Sts_Opened) OTU(Sts_LiftLower) OTU(Sts_LiftUpper) ,OTU(Sts_SIPCavity) OTU(Sts_SIPLower) OTU(Sts_SIPUpper) OTU(Sts_Pulsing) ,OTU(Sts_Moving) ,CLR(Val_Cmd) MOV(33,Val_Sts) CLR(Val_State) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ENUMERATED SOURCE / QUALITY VALUES
============================================================
Source and Quality for Input / Output values / status (SrcQ_IO)

0 = Good: live, confirmed good;   1 = Good: live, assumed good;
2 = Good: no feedback, assumed good;   8 = Test: Simulated;   9 = Test: Loopback;
10 = Test: Manually Entered;   16 = Uncertain: Live, off-spec;
17 = Uncertain, Substituted at Device / Bus;   18 = Uncertain, Substituted at AOI;
19 = Uncertain, using last known good;    20 = Uncertain, using replacement value;
32 = Bad, Signal Failure;   33 = Bad, Channel Fault;
34 = Bad, Module / Comms Fault;   35 = Bad, Invalid Configuration

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Added rung for Source/Quality enumerations.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[MOV(20,Wrk_SrcQ) ,XIC(Inp_IOFault) MOV(34,Wrk_SrcQ) ,MOV(Wrk_SrcQ,SrcQ_IO) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Source and Quality for primary values / status (SrcQ)

0 = Good: live, confirmed good;   1 = Good: live, assumed good;
2 = Good: no feedback, assumed good;   8 = Test: Simulated;   9 = Test: Loopback;
10 = Test: Manually Entered;   16 = Uncertain: Live, off-spec;
17 = Uncertain, Substituted at Device / Bus;   18 = Uncertain, Substituted at AOI;
19 = Uncertain, using last known good;    20 = Uncertain, using replacement value;
32 = Bad, Signal Failure;   33 = Bad, Channel Fault;
34 = Bad, Module / Comms Fault;   35 = Bad, Invalid Configuration

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Added rung for Source/Quality enumerations.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(20,SrcQ);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Clear the Alarms and the Notify Status, and show the Alarms Inhibited breadcrumb.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTU(Alm_Fail) OTU(Alm_IntlkTrip) OTU(Alm_IOFault) ,OTU(Sts_Fail) OTU(Sts_IntlkTrip) OTU(Sts_IOFault) ,OTL(Sts_AlmInh) CLR(Val_Notify) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="Logic" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Normal Scan: control / monitor mix proof valve]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Copyright © Rockwell Automation, Inc.  All Rights Reserved.
============================================================
P_ValveMP:  PROCESS -- MIX PROOF VALVE
============================================================
Revision 3.1-02 Release  2014-09-30:  See V3.1-xx Release Notes for details.
V2.x Revision History archived.
V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added Inf_Lib. Using P_Alarm, P_Mode V3.0.
V3.0-01  2013-07-31:  Modified Parameter descriptions only.
V3.0-02  2013-09-03:  Modified Parameter descriptions only.
V3.0-03  2013-10-30:  Corrected Parameter descriptions and
default configuration values for alarms only.
V3.1-00  2014-07-08:  Modified to use P_Alarm, P_Mode V3.1; fixed name of
PCmd_IOFaultSuppress. Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_Xxxxx),
source/quality values (SrcQ). Modified to consistently use alias tag names.
V3.1-01  2014-09-03:  Exposed fail timer ACC/PRE (read-only). Corrections to
Nrdy_  trip and reset logic. Using P_Alarm, P_Mode V3.1-01.
V3.1-02  2014-09-30:  Unchanged, but using P_Alarm V3.1-02.
============================================================
This Instruction controls and monitors a Mix Proof Valve.  This type of valve
uses dual seats and a leakage cavity in a single body to act as a one-piece
:"double block and bleed" valve setup.  The path from one side to the other
can be opened or closed, and each seat can be individually lifted for cleaning.
This instruction supports optional valve connections for CIP / SIP of the leakage
cavity, and SIP of the lower and upper seats, with outputs to open and close
separate cavity inlet (typ. steam) and cavity outlet valves.

This instruction also supports:
*  State model which ensures seats are sequenced to avoid cross-contamination
*  Monitoring of limit switch feedback, display of actual valve status
*  Detection of failure to reach the next required position in seat sequence
*  Monitoring of Permissive conditions to allow energizing
*  Monitoring of Interlock conditions to de-energize
*  Simulation, providing feedback of a working valve while disabling outputs
*  Monitoring of I/O communication faults
*  Alarms for Failure to reach position, Interlock Trip, I/O Fault
*  "Available" status for use by automation logic to know whether valve
      can be controlled by other objects.

Modes are provided by a P_Mode AOI instance.
Alarms are provided by P_Alarm AOI instances.
Modes of operation: Operator, Program, Override, Maintenance, Hand
============================================================
SHOW LOCAL STRINGS
============================================================
The STRINGs containing the text associated with each instance of this
instruction cannot be Input or Output Parameters, because STRINGs are not
 'atomic' types. (Inputs and Outputs must be SINT, INT, DINT, REAL, or BOOL.)

In order to make it easier to find and configure these STRINGs, this rung
was added.  THE JMP (and the LBL on the following rung)
MUST NOT BE REMOVED!!!

To view the STRINGs, go to the instruction instance (in LD or FBD), RIGHT-click
to bring up the context menu and select "Open Instruction Logic".
This rung will appear with the STRING values for the selected instance.
You may double-click the STRING values here to modify them as well.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[JMP(SkipText)CONCAT(Cfg_Desc,Cfg_Label,Cfg_Tag)LOWER(Inf_Lib,Inf_Type);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
MODE PROCESSING
============================================================
This rung handles received Mode Inputs and Commands:

NOTE:  All Commands for Mode, Alarm are aliased directly to the
corresponding Commands in the contained P_Mode and P_Alarm AOIs.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(SkipText)P_Mode(Mode);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung handles simple First-Come First-Served Ownership Arbitration.
If a requestor supplies a non-zero Owner ID and the current owner is NONE (zero),
Ownership is assigned to the requesting ID.  When that requestor sets the Owner ID back
to zero, Ownership is relinquished back to NONE.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[EQU(PSet_Owner,0) ,EQU(Val_Owner,0) ]MOV(PSet_Owner,Val_Owner);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
CONFIGURATION PROCESSING
============================================================
These rungs get Configuration data (such as timer presets) and distribute as needed.
Note that some Configuration data are used directly in-place.

Enter the time (in seconds) for the valve to successfully move from one state to the next
(along the path from current state to target state) before declaring a fault.

If the timer preset calcuated wraps negative (more than 2.14... million seconds), then max out the
Timer Preset.  Note that a negative timer preset will fault the controller!!!]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MUL(Cfg_FailT,1000,Wrk_FailT.PRE)XIC(Wrk_FailT.PRE.31)MOV(2147483647,Wrk_FailT.PRE)OTE(Err_Fail);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If any of the valve Feedback Timer presets is invalid (outside the range of
0 to 2147483647 ms), flag a Timer Configuration Error.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[LIM(2147483.1,Cfg_FdbkTimeTbl[0],-0.00000001) ,LIM(2147483.1,Cfg_FdbkTimeTbl[1],-0.00000001) ,LIM(2147483.1,Cfg_FdbkTimeTbl[2],-0.00000001) ,LIM(2147483.1,Cfg_FdbkTimeTbl[3],-0.00000001) ,LIM(2147483.1,Cfg_FdbkTimeTbl[4],-0.00000001) ,LIM(2147483.1,Cfg_FdbkTimeTbl[5],-0.00000001) ,LIM(2147483.1,Cfg_FdbkTimeTbl[6],-0.00000001) ,LIM(2147483.1,Cfg_FdbkTimeTbl[7],-0.00000001) ,LIM(2147483.1,Cfg_FdbkTimeTbl[8],-0.00000001) ,LIM(2147483.1,Cfg_FdbkTimeTbl[9],-0.00000001) ,LIM(2147483.1,Cfg_FdbkTimeTbl[10],-0.00000001) ,LIM(2147483.1,Cfg_PulseOpenT,-0.00000001) ,LIM(2147483.1,Cfg_PulseCloseT,-0.00000001) ]OTE(Err_Timer);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung generates a summary Bad Config status, simply an OR of the individual bits provided above
(in the Configuration handling section).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Err_Fail) ,XIC(Err_Timer) ,[XIC(Fail.Sts_Err) ,XIC(IntlkTrip.Sts_Err) ,XIC(IOFault.Sts_Err) ] OTE(Err_Alarm) ]OTE(Sts_Err);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
FEEDBACK INPUT GATHERING
============================================================
The feedback inputs are treated as a 6-bit word using word-wise logic in many
rungs that follow.  This rung gathers the separate inputs into that 6-bit word.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Inp_ClosedLS) OTE(Wrk_Inp.0) ,XIC(Inp_OpenLS) OTE(Wrk_Inp.1) ,XIC(Inp_LowerLS) OTE(Wrk_Inp.2) ,XIC(Inp_UpperLS) OTE(Wrk_Inp.3) ,XIC(Inp_CavityInLS) OTE(Wrk_Inp.4) ,XIC(Inp_CavityOutLS) OTE(Wrk_Inp.5) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
INTERLOCK / PERMISSIVE BYPASS / CHECK COMMAND HANDLING
============================================================
The Bypass Command bypasses the Bypassable Permissives and Interlocks.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(OCmd_Bypass)OTU(OCmd_Bypass)OTL(Wrk_Bypass);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Check Command enables checking of ALL
Permissives and Interlocks (cancels the bypass).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(OCmd_Check)OTU(OCmd_Check)OTU(Wrk_Bypass);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the internal Bypass flag is set, Bypassable Interlocks and Permissives ARE BYPASSED.
Bypassing is ACTIVE if Bypass selected OR in Maintenance Mode,
or in Override Mode if Override Bypassing is configured.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Wrk_Bypass) OTE(Sts_Bypass) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ,XIC(Sts_Ovrd) XIC(Cfg_OvrdPermIntlk) ]OTE(Sts_BypActive);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If a Maintenance Bypass function is active, display the Maintenance Bypass
Indicator (triangle symbol) on the graphic symbol.  Bypass functions are:
*  Interlock / Permissive Bypass function is enabled]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Sts_Bypass)OTE(Sts_MaintByp);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Ready for Interlock / Permissive Bypass if not bypassed.
Ready to cancel Bypass (resume checking) if bypassed.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Wrk_Bypass) OTE(Rdy_Bypass) ,XIC(Wrk_Bypass) OTE(Rdy_Check) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
DEVICE DISABLE/ENABLE COMMAND HANDLING
============================================================
The Disable Command disables the Analog Output.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(MCmd_Disable)OTU(MCmd_Disable)XIC(Mode.Rdy_MRel)OTL(Wrk_Disabled);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Enable Command cancels the Disable and enables the Analog Output.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(MCmd_Enable)OTU(MCmd_Enable)XIC(Mode.Rdy_MRel)OTU(Wrk_Disabled);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="14" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the internal Disabled flag is set, the valve is DISABLED.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_Disabled)OTE(Sts_Disabled);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="15" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Ready to Disable device if in Maintenance Mode and device is NOT Disabled.
Ready to Enable device if in Maintenance Mode and device IS Disabled.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Mode.Rdy_MRel)[XIO(Wrk_Disabled) OTE(Rdy_Disable) ,XIC(Wrk_Disabled) OTE(Rdy_Enable) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="16" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ALARM RESET COMMAND HANDLING
============================================================
This rung handles the Alarm Reset Input and Commands
and the "Reset and Ack All" Operator Command.

This rung processes received Reset Commands from:

1.  The Operator via HMI Operator Command, or
2.  Higher-level strategies via Program Command
3.  Pushbuttons or other block via Input
4.  Resets initiated by other device Operator Commands (if configured to do so)
and forwards the Reset to ALL Alarms and latched Shed conditions.

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####
#####  V3.1-01  2014-08-29:  Corrections to Nrdy_ trip and reset logic.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_Reset) OTU(OCmd_Reset) ,[XIC(OCmd_Close) ,XIC(OCmd_Open) ,XIC(OCmd_LiftLower) XIC(Cfg_HasLiftLower) ,XIC(OCmd_LiftUpper) XIC(Cfg_HasLiftUpper) ,XIC(OCmd_SIPCavity) XIC(Cfg_HasSIPCavity) ,XIC(OCmd_SIPLower) XIC(Cfg_HasSIPLower) ,XIC(OCmd_SIPUpper) XIC(Cfg_HasSIPUpper) ] XIC(Cfg_OCmdResets) [XIC(Sts_Oper) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ] ,XIC(OCmd_ResetAckAll) OTU(OCmd_ResetAckAll) [OTL(PCmd_FailAck) ,OTL(PCmd_IntlkTripAck) ,OTL(PCmd_IOFaultAck) ] ,XIC(PCmd_Reset) [XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear) OTU(PCmd_Reset) ,NOP() ] ,XIC(Inp_Reset) ][OTL(Fail.PCmd_Reset) OTL(IntlkTrip.PCmd_Reset) OTL(IOFault.PCmd_Reset) ,XIC(Sts_Fail) RES(Wrk_FailT) ,OTU(Nrdy_Fail) ,[XIO(Inp_IOFault) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) ] OTU(Nrdy_IOFault) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="17" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
VALVE COMMAND HANDLING
============================================================
This rung provides a "Permissives OK" bit for use in later rungs.
If permissives are NOT OK, the only thing that can be done with
the valve is to CLOSE it.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Inp_PermOK) ,XIC(Sts_BypActive) ]XIC(Inp_NBPermOK)OTE(Wrk_PermOK);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="18" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Valve is NOT READY to be opened and closed by automation if
interlocks are not OK, permissives are not OK (to go to a state other than CLOSED),
any FAULTS (position failure, I/O comm fail) exist, or the
valve is disabled or has a configuration error.

 If an interlock not OK caused the valve Target State
to CHANGE to CLOSE, show an Interlock Trip status (and possibly alarm).

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####
#####  V3.1-01  2014-08-29:  Corrections to Nrdy_ trip and reset logic.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTU(Nrdy_NoMode)[XIC(Sts_Disabled) OTE(Nrdy_Disabled) ,XIC(Sts_Err) OTE(Nrdy_CfgErr) ,[XIO(Inp_IntlkOK) XIO(Sts_BypActive) ,XIO(Inp_NBIntlkOK) ] [NEQ(Wrk_CmdState,1) OTE(Sts_IntlkTrip) ,OTE(Nrdy_Intlk) ] ,XIO(Wrk_PermOK) EQU(Wrk_CmdState,1) OTE(Nrdy_Perm) ,XIC(Inp_IOFault) XIO(Inp_Sim) OTE(Sts_IOFault) XIC(Cfg_ShedOnIOFault) OTL(Nrdy_IOFault) ]OTE(Wrk_NotRdy);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="19" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Valve is NOT READY to be opened and closed by automation if
interlocks are not OK, permissives are not OK (to go to a state other than CLOSED),
any FAULTS (position failure, I/O comm fail) exist, or the
valve is disabled or has a configuration error.

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####
#####  V3.1-01  2014-08-29:  Corrections to Nrdy_ trip and reset logic.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Wrk_NotRdy) ,XIC(Nrdy_Fail) ,XIC(Nrdy_IOFault) ]OTE(Sts_NotRdy);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="20" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The device is AVAILABLE to be controlled by other objects
if it IS in Program Mode and it IS NOT "Not Ready".]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Sts_Prog)XIO(Sts_NotRdy)OTE(Sts_Available);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="21" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If a Valve SIP UPPER command is received in Operator, Program or Maintenance
Mode, or if in Override Mode and the Override SIP UPPER pin is set, and
SIP UPPER is enabled in configuration, set the new target state to SIP UPPER (10).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_SIPUpper) OTU(OCmd_SIPUpper) [XIC(Sts_Oper) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ] ,XIC(PCmd_SIPUpper) [XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear) OTU(PCmd_SIPUpper) ,NOP() ] XIC(Sts_Prog) ,EQU(Inp_OvrdCmd,7) CLR(Inp_OvrdCmd) XIC(Sts_Ovrd) ,XIC(Sts_Hand) XOR(Wrk_Inp,Cfg_FdbkStateTbl[10],Wrk_InpCheck) AND(Wrk_InpCheck,Cfg_FdbkReqdTbl[10],Wrk_InpCheck) EQU(Wrk_InpCheck,0) ]XIC(Cfg_HasSIPUpper)XIO(Sts_NotRdy)XIC(Wrk_PermOK)[MOV(10,Wrk_CmdState) ,OTU(Wrk_Pulse) RES(Wrk_PulseT) ,MOV(10,Wrk_TgtState) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="22" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If a Valve SIP LOWER command is received in Operator, Program or Maintenance
Mode, or if in Override Mode and the Override SIP LOWER pin is set, and
SIP LOWER is enabled in configuration, set the new target state to SIP LOWER (8).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_SIPLower) OTU(OCmd_SIPLower) [XIC(Sts_Oper) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ] ,XIC(PCmd_SIPLower) [XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear) OTU(PCmd_SIPLower) ,NOP() ] XIC(Sts_Prog) ,EQU(Inp_OvrdCmd,6) CLR(Inp_OvrdCmd) XIC(Sts_Ovrd) ,XIC(Sts_Hand) XOR(Wrk_Inp,Cfg_FdbkStateTbl[8],Wrk_InpCheck) AND(Wrk_InpCheck,Cfg_FdbkReqdTbl[8],Wrk_InpCheck) EQU(Wrk_InpCheck,0) ]XIC(Cfg_HasSIPLower)XIC(Wrk_PermOK)XIC(Wrk_PermOK)[MOV(8,Wrk_CmdState) ,OTU(Wrk_Pulse) RES(Wrk_PulseT) ,MOV(8,Wrk_TgtState) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="23" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If a Valve SIP CAVITY command is received in Operator, Program or Maintenance
Mode, or if in Override Mode and the Override SIP CAVITY pin is set, and
SIP CAVITY is enabled in configuration, set the new target state to SIP CAVITY (6).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_SIPCavity) OTU(OCmd_SIPCavity) [XIC(Sts_Oper) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ] ,XIC(PCmd_SIPCavity) [XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear) OTU(PCmd_SIPCavity) ,NOP() ] XIC(Sts_Prog) ,EQU(Inp_OvrdCmd,5) CLR(Inp_OvrdCmd) XIC(Sts_Ovrd) ,XIC(Sts_Hand) XOR(Wrk_Inp,Cfg_FdbkStateTbl[6],Wrk_InpCheck) AND(Wrk_InpCheck,Cfg_FdbkReqdTbl[6],Wrk_InpCheck) EQU(Wrk_InpCheck,0) ]XIC(Cfg_HasSIPCavity)XIO(Sts_NotRdy)XIC(Wrk_PermOK)[MOV(6,Wrk_CmdState) ,MOV(6,Wrk_TgtState) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="24" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If a Valve LIFT UPPER command is received in Operator, Program or Maintenance
Mode, or if in Override Mode and the Override LIFT UPPER pin is set, and
LIFT UPPER is enabled in configuration, set the new target state to LIFT UPPER (5).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_LiftUpper) OTU(OCmd_LiftUpper) [XIC(Sts_Oper) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ] ,XIC(PCmd_LiftUpper) [XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear) OTU(PCmd_LiftUpper) ,NOP() ] XIC(Sts_Prog) ,EQU(Inp_OvrdCmd,4) CLR(Inp_OvrdCmd) XIC(Sts_Ovrd) ,XIC(Sts_Hand) XOR(Wrk_Inp,Cfg_FdbkStateTbl[5],Wrk_InpCheck) AND(Wrk_InpCheck,Cfg_FdbkReqdTbl[5],Wrk_InpCheck) EQU(Wrk_InpCheck,0) ]XIC(Cfg_HasLiftUpper)XIO(Sts_NotRdy)XIC(Wrk_PermOK)[MOV(5,Wrk_CmdState) ,OTU(Wrk_Pulse) RES(Wrk_PulseT) ,MOV(5,Wrk_TgtState) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="25" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If a Valve LIFT LOWER command is received in Operator, Program or Maintenance
Mode, or if in Override Mode and the Override LIFT LOWER pin is set, and
LIFT LOWER is enabled in configuration, set the new target state to LIFT LOWER (4).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_LiftLower) OTU(OCmd_LiftLower) [XIC(Sts_Oper) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ] ,XIC(PCmd_LiftLower) [XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear) OTU(PCmd_LiftLower) ,NOP() ] XIC(Sts_Prog) ,EQU(Inp_OvrdCmd,3) CLR(Inp_OvrdCmd) XIC(Sts_Ovrd) ,XIC(Sts_Hand) XOR(Wrk_Inp,Cfg_FdbkStateTbl[4],Wrk_InpCheck) AND(Wrk_InpCheck,Cfg_FdbkReqdTbl[4],Wrk_InpCheck) EQU(Wrk_InpCheck,0) ]XIC(Cfg_HasLiftLower)XIO(Sts_NotRdy)XIC(Wrk_PermOK)[MOV(4,Wrk_CmdState) ,OTU(Wrk_Pulse) RES(Wrk_PulseT) ,MOV(4,Wrk_TgtState) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="26" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If a Valve OPEN command is received in Operator, Program or Maintenance
Mode, or if in Override Mode and the Override OPEN pin is set,
set the new target state to OPEN (3).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_Open) OTU(OCmd_Open) [XIC(Sts_Oper) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ] ,XIC(PCmd_Open) [XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear) OTU(PCmd_Open) ,NOP() ] XIC(Sts_Prog) ,EQU(Inp_OvrdCmd,2) CLR(Inp_OvrdCmd) XIC(Sts_Ovrd) ,XIC(Sts_Hand) XOR(Wrk_Inp,Cfg_FdbkStateTbl[3],Wrk_InpCheck) AND(Wrk_InpCheck,Cfg_FdbkReqdTbl[3],Wrk_InpCheck) EQU(Wrk_InpCheck,0) ]XIO(Sts_NotRdy)XIC(Wrk_PermOK)[MOV(3,Wrk_CmdState) ,MOV(3,Wrk_TgtState) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="27" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If a Valve CLOSE command is received in Operator, Program or Maintenance
Mode, or if in Override Mode and the Override CLOSE pin is set,
set the new target state to CLOSE (1).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_Close) OTU(OCmd_Close) [XIC(Sts_Oper) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ] ,XIC(PCmd_Close) [XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear) OTU(PCmd_Close) ,NOP() ] XIC(Sts_Prog) ,EQU(Inp_OvrdCmd,1) CLR(Inp_OvrdCmd) XIC(Sts_Ovrd) ,XIC(Sts_Hand) [XOR(Wrk_Inp,Cfg_FdbkStateTbl[1],Wrk_InpCheck) AND(Wrk_InpCheck,Cfg_FdbkReqdTbl[1],Wrk_InpCheck) EQU(Wrk_InpCheck,0) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) ] ]XIO(Sts_NotRdy)[MOV(1,Wrk_CmdState) ,MOV(1,Wrk_TgtState) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="28" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If an Interlock that is not bypassed is NOT OK, or if the valve is disabled or
faulted, CLOSE the valve. 

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Sts_NotRdy)[MOV(1,Wrk_CmdState) ,MOV(1,Wrk_TgtState) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="29" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
LIMIT SWITCH FEEDBACK CHECK
============================================================
If the valve is NOT being simulated, check the feedback INPUTS that are configured
as REQURED for this (next) state against their configured requred STATES to see if
we've achieved the Next State (on our way to the Target State).

[The first branch is there to help ensure we don't fault the controller on an
invalid array index.  If the array index is outside the arrays (valid = 0 to 10),
then start over from the "intermediate -- de-energized" state (state 0)  ].]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[LIM(11,Wrk_NextState,-1) CLR(Wrk_NextState) ,XOR(Wrk_Inp,Cfg_FdbkStateTbl[Wrk_NextState],Wrk_InpCheck) AND(Wrk_InpCheck,Cfg_FdbkReqdTbl[Wrk_NextState],Wrk_InpCheck) ,MUL(Cfg_FdbkTimeTbl[Wrk_NextState],1000,Wrk_StateT.PRE) XIC(Wrk_StateT.PRE.31) CLR(Wrk_StateT.PRE) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="30" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the valve is NOT being simulated, once the Feedback Inputs that are required
reach their required states, start waiting the State Time for this state.
Once the time is done, we show the valve as "AT" the "next" state, and
it becomes the current state.  If the newly current state equals the 
Target state, we're done moving.

If the valve IS simulated, instead of checking the limit switch feedback,
we simply use the state time configured for this state, but make it a
minimum of 1 second, to simulate valve travel/confirm time between states.
(Simple but effective....)
(Don't worry, the State timer preset is written every scan in the rung above.
This overwrite will only happen in simulation.)

@@@@@  A timer is doubled to ensure it sets or clears the  @@@@@
@@@@@  .DN bit the same scan if the timer preset is zero.  @@@@@]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[[XIC(Inp_Sim) [LES(Wrk_StateT.PRE,1000) MOV(1000,Wrk_StateT.PRE) ,NOP() ] ,XIO(Inp_Sim) EQU(Wrk_InpCheck,0) ] TON(Wrk_StateT,?,?) TON(Wrk_StateT,?,?) ,XIC(Wrk_StateT.DN) MOV(Wrk_NextState,Wrk_CurrState) [OTE(Wrk_AtState) ,NEQ(Wrk_CurrState,Wrk_TgtState) RES(Wrk_StateT) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="31" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
VALVE POSITION FAILURE DETECTION
============================================================
Once we are trying to move, if we don't reach the NEXT state (along
the path to the TARGET state) within the failure time, the valve has failed.

If we are at the target position and lose the feedback, the valve has failed.

This rung runs the failure timer if the fail timer preset is greater than zero.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Wrk_AtState)GRT(Wrk_FailT.PRE,0)XIO(Sts_Maint)TON(Wrk_FailT,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="32" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the Valve Failure timer times out and we're not in Maintenance Mode,
raise an Alarm for Valve Failure (valve moved but did not reach target).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_FailT.DN)OTE(Sts_Fail);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="33" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
SHED ON FAULT LOGIC
============================================================
This rung handles latching in of conditions which are configured to cause
valve to close.

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Sts_Fail)XIC(Cfg_ShedOnFail)OTL(Nrdy_Fail);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="34" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
VALVE "PULSING" STATUS GENERATION
============================================================
NOTE: Most valve status bits are generated below.  This bit is generated
here because it is used within the device logic that follows.

If pulsing is enabled, run the pulse timer with the appropriate preset.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Cfg_PulseLiftLower) EQU(Wrk_CmdState,4) [EQU(Wrk_CurrState,4) ,EQU(Wrk_CurrState,0) ] ,XIC(Cfg_PulseLiftUpper) EQU(Wrk_CmdState,5) [EQU(Wrk_CurrState,5) ,EQU(Wrk_CurrState,0) ] ,XIC(Cfg_PulseSIPLower) EQU(Wrk_CmdState,8) [EQU(Wrk_CurrState,8) ,EQU(Wrk_CurrState,7) ,EQU(Wrk_CurrState,6) ] ,XIC(Cfg_PulseSIPUpper) EQU(Wrk_CmdState,10) [EQU(Wrk_CurrState,10) ,EQU(Wrk_CurrState,9) ,EQU(Wrk_CurrState,6) ] ]OTE(Sts_Pulsing);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="35" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
DEVICE COMMAND ENUMERATED VALUE
============================================================
Val_Cmd is the command currently being processed:
0 = None
1 = Close
3 = Open
4 = Lift Lower Seat
5 = Lift Upper Seat
6 = SIP/CIP Cavity
8 = SIP/CIP Lower Seat
10 = SIP/CIP Upper Seat]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[EQU(Wrk_CurrState,Wrk_CmdState) XIO(Sts_Pulsing) CLR(Val_Cmd) ,[NEQ(Wrk_CurrState,Wrk_CmdState) ,XIC(Sts_Pulsing) ] MOV(Wrk_CmdState,Val_Cmd) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="36" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
VALVE STATE DIAGRAM IMPLEMENTATION
============================================================
When the valve is MOVING, the following rungs determine the NEXT state
for the valve to move to, given the CURRENT state and the TARGET state.

See the State Diagram in the documentation for details.

CURRENT STATE = 0 (Intermediate: DE-ENERGIZED)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NEQ(Wrk_CurrState,Wrk_TgtState)EQU(Wrk_CurrState,0)[MOV(6,Wrk_NextState) ,EQU(Wrk_TgtState,1) MOV(1,Wrk_NextState) ,LIM(2,Wrk_TgtState,3) MOV(2,Wrk_NextState) ,EQU(Wrk_TgtState,4) MOV(4,Wrk_NextState) ,EQU(Wrk_TgtState,5) MOV(5,Wrk_NextState) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="37" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[CURRENT STATE = 1 (CLOSED)
CURRENT STATE = 2 (Intermediate: CLOSE CAVITY PRIOR TO OPENING)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NEQ(Wrk_CurrState,Wrk_TgtState)[EQU(Wrk_CurrState,1) MOV(0,Wrk_NextState) ,EQU(Wrk_CurrState,2) [MOV(0,Wrk_NextState) ,EQU(Wrk_TgtState,3) MOV(3,Wrk_NextState) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="38" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[CURRENT STATE = 3 (OPEN)
CURRENT STATE = 4 (LIFT LOWER)
CURRENT STATE = 5 (LIFT UPPER)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NEQ(Wrk_CurrState,Wrk_TgtState)[EQU(Wrk_CurrState,3) MOV(2,Wrk_NextState) ,EQU(Wrk_CurrState,4) MOV(0,Wrk_NextState) ,EQU(Wrk_CurrState,5) MOV(0,Wrk_NextState) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="39" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[CURRENT STATE = 6 (SIP/CIP CAVITY)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NEQ(Wrk_CurrState,Wrk_TgtState)EQU(Wrk_CurrState,6)[MOV(0,Wrk_NextState) ,LIM(7,Wrk_TgtState,8) MOV(7,Wrk_NextState) ,LIM(9,Wrk_TgtState,10) MOV(9,Wrk_NextState) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="40" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[CURRENT STATE = 7 (intermediate: LIFT LOWER PRIOR TO SIP/CIP LOWER)
CURRENT STATE = 8 (SIP/CIP LOWER)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NEQ(Wrk_CurrState,Wrk_TgtState)[EQU(Wrk_CurrState,7) [MOV(6,Wrk_NextState) ,EQU(Wrk_TgtState,8) MOV(8,Wrk_NextState) ] ,EQU(Wrk_CurrState,8) MOV(7,Wrk_NextState) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="41" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[CURRENT STATE = 9 (intermediate: LIFT UPPER PRIOR TO SIP/CIP UPPER)
CURRENT STATE = 10 (SIP/CIP UPPER)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NEQ(Wrk_CurrState,Wrk_TgtState)[EQU(Wrk_CurrState,9) [MOV(6,Wrk_NextState) ,EQU(Wrk_TgtState,10) MOV(10,Wrk_NextState) ] ,EQU(Wrk_CurrState,10) MOV(9,Wrk_NextState) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="42" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
SET VALVE OUTPUTS
============================================================
Based on the configuration of the Output State Table,
set the Outputs to their configured states for the Next State determined above.
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(Cfg_OutStateTbl[Wrk_NextState],Wrk_Out);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="43" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the valve is NOT in simulation, set the output bits to the pattern retrieved above.
(Outputs are ALL DE-ENERGIZED in simulation.)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Inp_Sim)[XIC(Wrk_Out.0) OTE(Out_Close) ,XIC(Wrk_Out.1) OTE(Out_Open) ,XIC(Wrk_Out.2) OTE(Out_LiftLower) ,XIC(Wrk_Out.3) OTE(Out_LiftUpper) ,XIC(Wrk_Out.4) OTE(Out_CavityInlet) ,XIC(Wrk_Out.5) OTE(Out_CavityOutlet) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="44" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
VALVE PULSE HANDLING
============================================================
These rungs handle the pulsing of seat lifts when so configured (see Cfg_PulseXxxx bits).

If pulsing is NOT configured (or becomes not configured), the Commanded State
becomes the Target State for that lift / SIP / CIP.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[EQU(Wrk_CmdState,4) XIO(Cfg_PulseLiftLower) ,EQU(Wrk_CmdState,5) XIO(Cfg_PulseLiftUpper) ,EQU(Wrk_CmdState,8) XIO(Cfg_PulseSIPLower) ,EQU(Wrk_CmdState,10) XIO(Cfg_PulseSIPUpper) ]MOV(Wrk_CmdState,Wrk_TgtState)OTU(Wrk_Pulse)RES(Wrk_PulseT);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="45" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If pulsing is enabled, run the pulse timer with the appropriate preset.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Sts_Pulsing)[XIO(Wrk_Pulse) MUL(Cfg_PulseOpenT,1000,Wrk_PulseT.PRE) ,XIC(Wrk_Pulse) MUL(Cfg_PulseCloseT,1000,Wrk_PulseT.PRE) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="46" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_PulseT.PRE.31)CLR(Wrk_PulseT.PRE);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="47" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[@@@@@  A timer is doubled to ensure it sets or clears the  @@@@@
@@@@@  .DN bit the same scan if the timer preset is zero.  @@@@@]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Sts_Pulsing)TON(Wrk_PulseT,?,?)TON(Wrk_PulseT,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="48" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If pulsing is enabled, the Target State is reached and the Pulse Time is complete,
switch to the "OTHER" Target State   ( 4 - 0 - 4;  5 - 0 - 5;  8 - 6 - 6;  10 - 6 - 10 ).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_PulseT.DN)[EQU(Wrk_CmdState,4) [EQU(Wrk_TgtState,4) EQU(Wrk_CurrState,4) OTL(Wrk_Pulse) MOV(0,Wrk_TgtState) ,EQU(Wrk_TgtState,0) EQU(Wrk_CurrState,0) OTU(Wrk_Pulse) MOV(4,Wrk_TgtState) ] ,EQU(Wrk_CmdState,5) [EQU(Wrk_TgtState,5) EQU(Wrk_CurrState,5) OTL(Wrk_Pulse) MOV(0,Wrk_TgtState) ,EQU(Wrk_TgtState,0) EQU(Wrk_CurrState,0) OTU(Wrk_Pulse) MOV(5,Wrk_TgtState) ] ,EQU(Wrk_CmdState,8) [EQU(Wrk_TgtState,8) EQU(Wrk_CurrState,8) OTL(Wrk_Pulse) MOV(6,Wrk_TgtState) ,EQU(Wrk_TgtState,6) EQU(Wrk_CurrState,6) OTU(Wrk_Pulse) MOV(8,Wrk_TgtState) ] ,EQU(Wrk_CmdState,10) [EQU(Wrk_TgtState,10) EQU(Wrk_CurrState,10) OTL(Wrk_Pulse) MOV(6,Wrk_TgtState) ,EQU(Wrk_TgtState,6) EQU(Wrk_CurrState,6) OTU(Wrk_Pulse) MOV(10,Wrk_TgtState) ] ]RES(Wrk_PulseT);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="49" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
REMAINING STATUS
============================================================
These rungs generate the Valve Position Status bits.
If the valve has ACHIEVED THE TARGET POSITION
(it has reached a state and that state is the Target State),
then show the position based on the State Diagram
(see documentation).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Wrk_AtState) EQU(Wrk_CurrState,Wrk_TgtState) ,XIC(Sts_Pulsing) ][EQU(Wrk_CurrState,1) OTE(Sts_Closed) ,EQU(Wrk_CurrState,3) OTE(Sts_Opened) ,[EQU(Wrk_CurrState,4) ,XIC(Sts_Pulsing) EQU(Wrk_CmdState,4) ] OTE(Sts_LiftLower) ,[EQU(Wrk_CurrState,5) ,XIC(Sts_Pulsing) EQU(Wrk_CmdState,5) ] OTE(Sts_LiftUpper) ,EQU(Wrk_CurrState,6) OTE(Sts_SIPCavity) ,[EQU(Wrk_CurrState,8) ,XIC(Sts_Pulsing) EQU(Wrk_CmdState,8) ] OTE(Sts_SIPLower) ,[EQU(Wrk_CurrState,10) ,XIC(Sts_Pulsing) EQU(Wrk_CmdState,10) ] OTE(Sts_SIPUpper) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="50" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Any time the CURRENT valve state is NOT equal to the TARGET state,
the valve is considered MOVING.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Sts_Pulsing)[NEQ(Wrk_CurrState,Wrk_TgtState) ,XIO(Wrk_AtState) ]OTE(Sts_Moving);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="51" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
OTHER VALUES
============================================================
Indicate the Actual Valve Internal State for animating the State
Diagram on the HMI Faceplate.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(Wrk_CurrState,Val_State);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="52" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Val_Sts is the current device status, as determined by this AOI,
based on its knowledge of commands executed and feedback.
(This is the status that should be monitored by, for example, FT Historian.)
0 = Powerup / Unknown (Hand Mode with no feedback, for example)
1 = Closed
3 = Opened
4 = Lower Seat Lifted
5 = Upper Seat Lifted
6 = SIP/CIP Cavity
8 = SIP/CIP Lower Seat
10 = SIP/CIP Upper Seat
11 = Moving
12 = Pulse SIP/CIP Lower Seat
13 = Pulse SIP/CIP Upper Seat
33 = Device Disabled

Val_Fault is the current device fault status, as determined by this AOI,
based on its knowledge of commands executed and feedback.
(This is the fault status that should be monitored by, for example, FT Historian.)
0 = None
16 = Position Fail
32 = I/O Fault (from Input)
34 = Configuration Error

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[CLR(Wrk_Sts) CLR(Wrk_Fault) ,XIC(Sts_Closed) MOV(1,Wrk_Sts) ,XIC(Sts_Opened) MOV(3,Wrk_Sts) ,XIC(Sts_LiftLower) MOV(4,Wrk_Sts) ,XIC(Sts_LiftUpper) MOV(5,Wrk_Sts) ,XIC(Sts_SIPCavity) MOV(6,Wrk_Sts) ,XIC(Sts_SIPLower) MOV(8,Wrk_Sts) ,XIC(Sts_SIPUpper) MOV(10,Wrk_Sts) ,XIC(Sts_Moving) MOV(11,Wrk_Sts) ,XIC(Sts_Pulsing) [XIC(Sts_SIPLower) MOV(12,Wrk_Sts) ,XIC(Sts_SIPUpper) MOV(13,Wrk_Sts) ] ,XIC(Nrdy_Fail) MOV(16,Wrk_Fault) ,XIC(Nrdy_IOFault) MOV(32,Wrk_Fault) ,XIC(Wrk_Disabled) MOV(33,Wrk_Sts) ,XIC(Sts_Err) MOV(34,Wrk_Fault) ,MOV(Wrk_Sts,Val_Sts) MOV(Wrk_Fault,Val_Fault) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="53" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ENUMERATED SOURCE / QUALITY VALUES
============================================================
Source and Quality for Input / Output values / status (SrcQ_IO)

0 = Good: live, confirmed good;   1 = Good: live, assumed good;
2 = Good: no feedback, assumed good;   8 = Test: Simulated;   9 = Test: Loopback;
10 = Test: Manually Entered;   16 = Uncertain: Live, off-spec;
17 = Uncertain, Substituted at Device / Bus;   18 = Uncertain, Substituted at AOI;
19 = Uncertain, using last known good;    20 = Uncertain, using replacement value;
32 = Bad, Signal Failure;   33 = Bad, Channel Fault;
34 = Bad, Module / Comms Fault;   35 = Bad, Invalid Configuration

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Added rung for Source/Quality enumerations.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[CLR(Wrk_SrcQ) ,XIC(Inp_IOFault) MOV(34,Wrk_SrcQ) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) MOV(9,Wrk_SrcQ) ,MOV(Wrk_SrcQ,SrcQ_IO) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="54" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Source and Quality for primary values / status (SrcQ)

0 = Good: live, confirmed good;   1 = Good: live, assumed good;
2 = Good: no feedback, assumed good;   8 = Test: Simulated;   9 = Test: Loopback;
10 = Test: Manually Entered;   16 = Uncertain: Live, off-spec;
17 = Uncertain, Substituted at Device / Bus;   18 = Uncertain, Substituted at AOI;
19 = Uncertain, using last known good;    20 = Uncertain, using replacement value;
32 = Bad, Signal Failure;   33 = Bad, Channel Fault;
34 = Bad, Module / Comms Fault;   35 = Bad, Invalid Configuration

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Added rung for Source/Quality enumerations.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(SrcQ_IO,SrcQ);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="55" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
OPERATOR COMMAND READIES
============================================================
Generally, the valve is ready for a new state command if it is not already targeted
at that state, if the permissives and interlocks (subject to bypassing) allow it,
the valve is in Operator or Maintenance Mode, and the valve is not
disabled or faulted.

#####  V3.1-01  2014-08-29:  Corrections to Nrdy_ trip and reset logic.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Sts_Oper) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ]XIO(Wrk_NotRdy)[XIO(Sts_NotRdy) ,XIC(Cfg_OCmdResets) ][NEQ(Wrk_CmdState,1) OTE(Rdy_Close) ,XIC(Wrk_PermOK) [NEQ(Wrk_CmdState,3) OTE(Rdy_Open) ,XIC(Cfg_HasLiftLower) NEQ(Wrk_CmdState,4) OTE(Rdy_LiftLower) ,XIC(Cfg_HasLiftUpper) NEQ(Wrk_CmdState,5) OTE(Rdy_LiftUpper) ,XIC(Cfg_HasSIPCavity) NEQ(Wrk_CmdState,6) OTE(Rdy_SIPCavity) ,XIC(Cfg_HasSIPLower) NEQ(Wrk_CmdState,8) OTE(Rdy_SIPLower) ,XIC(Cfg_HasSIPUpper) NEQ(Wrk_CmdState,10) OTE(Rdy_SIPUpper) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="56" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ALARM PROCESSING
============================================================
Pass the Cfg_PCmdClear configuration down to each P_Alarm instance.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear)OTE(Fail.Cfg_PCmdClear)OTE(IntlkTrip.Cfg_PCmdClear)OTE(IOFault.Cfg_PCmdClear);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="57" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The various alarms are ALWAYS allowed to Exist (Cfg_HasXxxAlarm can be 1), EXCEPT:
* If the valve DOES NOT CHECK ANY FEEDBACKS, the Fail alarm will never occur
and should not exist.  (If any feedback is checked, the Fail alarm must be allowed to exist.)

#####  V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added PCfg_AllowExist on P_Alarm 3.0.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTL(IntlkTrip.PCfg_AllowExist) OTL(IOFault.PCfg_AllowExist) ,[NEQ(Cfg_FdbkReqdTbl[0],0) ,NEQ(Cfg_FdbkReqdTbl[1],0) ,NEQ(Cfg_FdbkReqdTbl[2],0) ,NEQ(Cfg_FdbkReqdTbl[3],0) ,NEQ(Cfg_FdbkReqdTbl[4],0) ,NEQ(Cfg_FdbkReqdTbl[5],0) ,NEQ(Cfg_FdbkReqdTbl[6],0) ,NEQ(Cfg_FdbkReqdTbl[7],0) ,NEQ(Cfg_FdbkReqdTbl[8],0) ,NEQ(Cfg_FdbkReqdTbl[9],0) ,NEQ(Cfg_FdbkReqdTbl[10],0) ] OTE(Fail.PCfg_AllowExist) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="58" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Handle Valve Failed to Reach Target Position Alarm Processing using the standard P_Alarm AOI.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[P_Alarm(Fail);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="59" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Handle Interlock Trip Alarm Processing using the standard P_Alarm AOI.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[P_Alarm(IntlkTrip);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="60" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Handle I/O Fault Alarm Processing using the standard P_Alarm AOI.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[P_Alarm(IOFault);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="61" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If ANY alarm is Disabled, Inhibited or Suppressed, set the Alarm Inhibit
summary status bit (which puts the "I" box on the graphic symbol).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Fail.Sts_AlmInh) ,XIC(IntlkTrip.Sts_AlmInh) ,XIC(IOFault.Sts_AlmInh) ]OTE(Sts_AlmInh);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="62" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
NOTIFICATION VALUE
============================================================
Indicate the current alarm notification level as the max of any of the alarms,
and set the low-order bit for reset or ack required:
0 = Not in alarm, acknowledged
1 = Not in alarm, unacknowledged or reset required
2 = Low severity alarm, acknowledged
3 = Low severity alarm, unacknowledged
4 = Medium severity alarm, acknowledged
5 = Medium severity alarm, unacknowledged
6 = High severity alarm, acknowledged
7 = High severity alarm, unacknowledged
8 = Urgent severity alarm, acknowledged
9 = Urgent severity alarm, unacknowledged

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Separated Reset Reqd functions from Val_Notify  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[CLR(Wrk_Notify) ,GRT(Fail.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) MOV(Fail.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) ,GRT(IntlkTrip.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) MOV(IntlkTrip.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) ,GRT(IOFault.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) MOV(IOFault.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) ,[XIC(Fail.Val_Notify.0) ,XIC(IntlkTrip.Val_Notify.0) ,XIC(IOFault.Val_Notify.0) ] OTE(Wrk_Notify.0) ,MOV(Wrk_Notify,Val_Notify) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="63" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung identifies:
* if any alarm reset or other reset is required; and
* if any reset or acknowledge from the operator is required.

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx), split from Val_Notify logic (above).  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[[XIC(Fail.Rdy_Ack) ,XIC(IntlkTrip.Rdy_Ack) ,XIC(IOFault.Rdy_Ack) ] ,[XIC(Fail.Rdy_Reset) ,XIC(IntlkTrip.Rdy_Reset) ,XIC(IOFault.Rdy_Reset) ,XIC(Nrdy_Fail) ,XIC(Nrdy_IOFault) XIO(Sts_IOFault) ] OTE(Rdy_Reset) ]OTE(Rdy_ResetAckAll);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="Prescan" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Clear Ownership, set target to Closed state, actual to de-energized state, clear "lurking" Commands]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
PRESCAN (POWERUP) HANDLING
============================================================
On Prescan, set the Ownership to NO OWNER (0).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CLR(PSet_Owner)CLR(Val_Owner);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA["Lurking" Program Commands are cleared if they are set as "Edge" triggered
(cleared by this object as received).
(Lurking Acknowledge Commands are left to perform their action.)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear)[OTU(PCmd_Close) OTU(PCmd_Open) OTU(PCmd_LiftLower) OTU(PCmd_LiftUpper) ,OTU(PCmd_SIPCavity) OTU(PCmd_SIPLower) OTU(PCmd_SIPUpper) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA["Lurking" Operator Commands are cleared, as well as Program Reset.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTU(OCmd_Close) OTU(OCmd_Open) OTU(OCmd_LiftLower) OTU(OCmd_LiftUpper) ,OTU(OCmd_SIPCavity) OTU(OCmd_SIPLower) OTU(OCmd_SIPUpper) ,OTU(OCmd_Bypass) OTU(OCmd_Check) OTU(MCmd_Disable) OTU(MCmd_Enable) ,OTU(OCmd_Reset) OTU(OCmd_ResetAckAll) OTU(PCmd_Reset) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Override Command is set to NONE.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CLR(Inp_OvrdCmd);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Set the valve to its DE-ENERGIZED STATE and set TARGET state to CLOSED.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CLR(Wrk_CurrState)MOV(1,Wrk_TgtState)MOV(1,Wrk_CmdState)MOV(1,Wrk_NextState);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Clear the latched Shed faults.

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTU(Nrdy_Fail)OTU(Nrdy_IOFault);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Outputs are cleared on Prescan.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTU(Out_Close) OTU(Out_Open) OTU(Out_LiftLower) OTU(Out_LiftUpper) ,OTU(Out_CavityInlet) OTU(Out_CavityOutlet) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Show the enumerated valve command as NONE.
Show the enumerated valve status as POWERUP / UNKNOWN.
Show the internal valve state as DE-ENERGIZED.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CLR(Val_Cmd)CLR(Val_Sts)CLR(Val_State);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
<Dependencies>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_40"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_20"/>
<Dependency Type="AddOnInstructionDefinition" Name="P_Alarm"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_12"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_16"/>
<Dependency Type="AddOnInstructionDefinition" Name="P_Mode"/>
</Dependencies>
</AddOnInstructionDefinition>
</AddOnInstructionDefinitions>
</Controller>
</RSLogix5000Content>
